+++
title = "Stack bus headers"
[part.J5]
footprint = "Connector_PinHeader_2.54mm:PinHeader_2x06_P2.54mm_Vertical"
[part.J6]
footprint = "Connector_PinHeader_2.54mm:PinHeader_2x06_P2.54mm_Vertical"
+++
                                       +3V3
   +--------------------------+         |
   |                +-----+   |         |                         +-----+
   |    [ENC_SCK]--1|     |2--+         |          +-------------1|     |2--[VM_SENSE]
   |   [ENC_DATA]--3|     |4--[ENC_TX]  |          |  [TMC_CSN]--3|     |4--[TMC_SLEEPN]
   |    [ENC_CSQ]--5|     |6------------+          *-------------5|     |6--[TMC_SCK]
   |  [TMC_DIAG1]--7|     |8--[TMC_DIAG0]          |  [TMC_SDO]--7|     |8--[TMC_SDI]
   |    [TMC_ENN]--9|     |10-[ENC_IFA]            *-------------9|     |10-[TMC_REFL]
   |    [ENC_IFB]-11|     |12-[ENC_IFC]            *------------11|     |12-[TMC_REFR]
   |                +-----+                        |              +-----+
   |                 J5                            |               J6
  GND                Stack 2x06                   GND              Stack 2x06


    Every board carries J5 and J6 at the same place and rotation, so the boards stack in any order.
    Seen from the top: J5 at the top edge, odd row toward the board center; J6 at the bottom edge, even row toward it; pin 1 left.
    Signals take the inner rows where they can, GND the outer rows. Each group sits in the order its chip's pins leave toward it,
    so the fan-outs need no crossings: TMC SPI, SLEEPN, REFL and REFR leave the TMC5241's bottom edge toward J6;
    DIAG0, DIAG1, ENN and the encoder lines go to J5. One +3V3 pin carries the encoder and the TMC5241 logic (tens of mA).
    Header pins pass through each board: a board leaves the lines it does not use unwired.
    48 V never crosses the stack (VM_SENSE is the divided reading).
